{0 Limits}

Cloudflare Workers limits apply to deployed workero workers. Local [workerd]
tests do not establish what a deployment can consume. For the current values,
see the {{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/}Cloudflare
Workers limits}.

{1 Bundle size}

Cloudflare limits the uncompressed Worker bundle to 64 MiB on both Free and
Paid plans. It does not set a compressed bundle-size limit. Use
[wrangler deploy --outdir bundled/ --dry-run] to inspect the [Total Upload]
size before deployment. See
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/#worker-size}Worker
size}.

{1 Memory}

Cloudflare allows 128 MB of memory per isolate, including the JavaScript heap
and WebAssembly allocations. An isolate can handle multiple requests, so this
is not a per-request budget. See
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/#memory}Memory}.

{1 CPU time}

The CPU-time limit depends on the plan and trigger type. Cloudflare lists 10 ms
per HTTP request on the Free plan and a default of 30 seconds per HTTP request
on the Paid plan, configurable up to 5 minutes. Waiting on network requests
does not count as CPU time. See
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/#cpu-time}CPU time}.
